Section: Civil Time from Unix Seconds

 Seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC to the proleptic Gregorian date and time
 (H. Hinnant's civil_from_days), correct before 1970 as well.

  dt-civil-of-unix : Integer -> DateTime
  dt-civil-of-unix (secs) =
    let days = dt-floor-div secs seconds-per-day
    in let tod = secs - days * seconds-per-day
    in let z = days + 719468
    in let era = dt-floor-div z 146097
    in let doe = z - era * 146097
    in let yoe = (doe - doe / 1460 + doe / 36524 - doe / 146096) / 365
    in let doy = doe - (365 * yoe + yoe / 4 - yoe / 100)
    in let mp = (5 * doy + 2) / 153
    in let d = doy - (153 * mp + 2) / 5 + 1
    in let m = if mp < 10 then mp + 3 else mp - 9
    in DateTime {
      year = yoe + era * 400 + (if m <= 2 then 1 else 0),
      month = __narrow m,
      day = __narrow d,
      hour = __narrow (tod / 3600),
      minute = __narrow ((tod - (tod / 3600) * 3600) / 60),
      second = __narrow (tod - (tod / 60) * 60)
    }

 The X.509 validity clock (X509Chain x509-valid-at, TlsEndpoint cal-now):
 YYYYMMDDHHMMSS in UTC as fourteen ASCII digit bytes.

  unix-to-x509-now : Integer -> List Integer
  unix-to-x509-now (secs) =
    let c = dt-civil-of-unix secs
    in dt-digits (c.year) 4 & dt-digits (c.month) 2 & dt-digits (c.day) 2 & dt-digits (c.hour) 2 & dt-digits (c.minute) 2 & dt-digits (c.second) 2

  dt-digits : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  dt-digits (v) (n) = if n <= 0 then [] else dt-digits (v / 10) (n - 1) & [48 + (v - (v / 10) * 10)]